.TH "Docv::Term::Input" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Term::Input \- Turns raw events into the derived events a viewer consumes: the key pressed\-set, text\-versus\-command classification, clicks and multi\-clicks, drag lifecycle, scroll accumulation and pointer enter, move and leave.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Term::Input\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Turns raw events into the derived events a viewer consumes: the key
pressed\-set, text\-versus\-command classification, clicks and
multi\-clicks, drag lifecycle, scroll accumulation and pointer
enter, move and leave. Mouse pixel coordinates convert to cells with the current
cell size.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBCLICK_TIME = 500.milliseconds\fR
Longest press that still counts as a click.
.TP 4
\fBMULTI_CLICK_TIME = 400.milliseconds\fR
Longest gap between clicks of a multi\-click.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.PP
\fBdef cell_height : Int32\fR
.PP
\fBdef cell_height=(cell_height : Int32)\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef cell_width : Int32\fR
Cell size in pixels (from the window size or terminal reports).
.TP 4
\fBdef cell_width=(cell_width : Int32)\fR
Cell size in pixels (from the window size or terminal reports).
.TP 4
\fBdef feed(bytes : Bytes, & : Derived \-> ) : Nil\fR
Decodes \fIbytes\fR and yields derived events.
.TP 4
\fBdef flush : Nil\fR
Resolves buffered input after a timeout (a lone ESC).
.PP
\fBdef held : Hash(Int32,Docv::Term::Input::Held)\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef pending? : Bool\fR
True while bytes of an incomplete sequence wait for more input.
.TP 4
\fBdef pixels=(pixels : Bool)\fR
True when mouse reports carry pixels (mode 1016 is active).
.TP 4
\fBdef pixels? : Bool\fR
True when mouse reports carry pixels (mode 1016 is active).
.TP 4
\fBdef window(rows : Int32, cols : Int32, width : Int32, height : Int32) : Nil\fR
Sets the cell size from the window\(aqs pixel and cell extents.
